From ac44b21fc634791586be0e929f8d7c0eb13bfe0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:10:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/11] ASoC: qcom: run speaker protection in codec DMA lane order

The SP/VI code assumed speaker n is codec DMA lane n and that link codec
order is speaker order. On Glymur the WSA lanes alternate between the
WSA and WSA2 macros, so four amplifiers in link order sit on lanes 0, 2,
1, 3, while the factory R0/T0 and the per-speaker SP/VI tuning are kept
in lane order: speakers 1 and 2 got each other's calibration and tuning.

The machine driver now registers the VI speakers sorted by lane, from
"qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes", and fails the card on a property that is not
a permutation matching the speaker count. Audioreach keeps each
speaker's lane, builds the VI channel map in speaker order (resent
after the static cfg blob, which may carry its own), has the MFC before
SP RX output speaker order and requires an MFC after SP to restore lane
order, and refuses SP RX/VI without a matching speaker map.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
