From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:11:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/11] ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: add a V/I guard: no PA without V/I
 sense

Speaker protection estimates coil temperature and excursion from the
amplifier's V/I sense; without that stream the DSP protects the speaker
with stale or no data. With "qcom,vi-guard" the amplifier only runs its
PA while its own V/I sense port streams:

- unmute keeps the PA off unless VISENSE is enabled and prepared;
- the PA is switched off at VISENSE PRE_DEPREP;
- a 20 ms watchdog switches it off if the port stops or the amplifier
  detaches, and the off write must read back as off;
- a trip stays latched until the next stream start.

