A V/I capture with no 'WSA_AIF_VI Mixer' input enabled gives speaker
protection no feedback, but hw_params accepts it. Fail it with a clear
message, and lock the mixer from AIF_VI hw_params to hw_free so V/I
feedback cannot be switched off under a running speaker protection
graph.

The mixer state and the AIF_VI reservation share one lock. Since the
DAPM update in the mixer put takes the card locks, it runs after that
lock is dropped, and hw_params refuses a V/I capture while a put is
still in progress. Fold the per-TX bit handling of the put into one
path.

