From b570df6774267b1e7cd92af1b6c2bb576d779542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:12:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/11] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: configure SP RX and SP VI in one
 checked pass

SP RX and SP VI are configured from global state (operation mode,
speaker map) that can change between the two modules' media format
calls, and nothing checks that a WSA RX graph configured both.

Make a WSA RX backend prepare one speaker protection configuration
pass: mode and speaker map are snapshotted at its start, a pass that
configures only one of SP RX and SP VI fails the prepare, and either
module configured outside a pass is refused. A machine driver can
require speaker protection (audioreach_sp_set_required()); a WSA RX
graph without both modules then fails its prepare.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c       | 134 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h       |   4 +
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c |   8 ++
